# Made-up byte table for yomineko's synthetic framed-message test ROM. Not from any game.
# Every byte from 0x80 up is a character, so text can only be told from data by its frame.
# There is no katakana he or ri: katakana words use the hiragana codes. <name48> is a byte
# that stands for a name from memory. Bytes 40 and 41 stand for fixed words that the test
# ROM itself holds (encoding.rom_strings in the profile), so they are not in this file.
48=<name48>
60=。
61=！
62=？
63=…
7F=　
80=ぁ
81=あ
82=ぃ
83=い
84=ぅ
85=う
